    "profile_text": {
        "body": "AeroVironment is a public company, traded as AVAV, headquartered in Arlington, Virginia. According to its own site, it is a manufacturer of Unmanned Aircraft Systems, Unmanned Aerial Vehicles, Loitering Munition Systems, and Unmanned Ground Vehicles used for surveillance and reconnaissance by the United States Military, U.S. allies, and commercial industries. The company also says it manufactures High-Altitude Pseudo-Satellites.\n\nThe site describes MacCready Works as AeroVironment's advanced development group, which it says turns concepts into mission-ready autonomous systems. The group is named for Dr. Paul B. MacCready, Jr., and the company says its engineers, roboticists, and AI researchers design next-generation robotic systems across air, land, and sea. AeroVironment describes its approach as the MacCready Method, build fast, test relentlessly, deploy advantage, with small multidisciplinary teams working to move ideas into operational capability in months.\n\nThe company's legal exposure is recorded in Virginia, with a count of 152. No product listings, lawsuits, or MCP servers are held for it.",
